.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Felix Bloch&#x27;s theorem turns the Schrodinger equation for an electron in an infinite periodic crystal into a finite eigenvalue problem H(k) u_{nk} = E_n(k) u_{nk} at each crystal momentum k, periodic on the Brillouin zone. Hamiltonian builds H(k) by Bloch-summing real-space hoppings, and bands diagonalizes it -- reproducing the monatomic chain&#x27;s exact dispersion E(k) = -2t\cos k with no continuum limit or approximation involved.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/condensed/tight_binding/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_bloch_bands_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/condensed/tight_binding/plot_bloch_bands`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Bloch's Theorem: From an Infinite Chain to H(k)</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/condensed/tight_binding/plot_bloch_bands`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Slater and Koster showed how to build realistic band structures from a minimal empirical basis: a linear combination of atomic orbitals (LCAO), with hopping matrix elements between orbitals treated as fitting parameters rather than computed from first principles. Lattice and Hamiltonian are a direct, general-purpose realization of this philosophy: declare orbitals, declare empirical hoppings between them, and Bloch-sum the result into a multi-band H(k).">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/condensed/tight_binding/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_slater_koster_bands_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/condensed/tight_binding/plot_slater_koster_bands`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Slater-Koster LCAO: Empirical Multi-Orbital Band Structure</div>
    </div>


